From 1d392574aa9f652215d29f19cedf80a60d737f80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taehyun Kim <dice.thkim@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 00:12:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/20] SCUMM: Draw Korean TTF text a run at a time

Handing the font one glyph at a time forces every character onto the
game's own grid: the advance gets rounded to a game pixel, the dirty
rectangle has to be widened by hand, and each glyph is positioned
independently of its neighbours. Collect the characters into a run and
let drawString() lay them out instead.

A run ends when the caller moves elsewhere, changes colour, or drifts
too far from where the font would have put the next glyph, so per
character colour changes still work - they just split the line into
several runs. Enabled with "mode=string" in the [render] section.

This also fixes the punctuation placement. The engine positions single
byte characters against the ascii font and double byte ones against the
CJK font, and the height difference between the two bitmap fonts used
to cancel out. One TrueType face draws both, so the correction has to
go: single byte characters now share the line the Hangul established,
instead of landing on a baseline half a line further down.
---
 engines/scumm/charset.cpp | 158 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 engines/scumm/charset.h   |   3 +
 engines/scumm/gfx.cpp     |   8 ++
 engines/scumm/scumm.h     |  15 ++++
 4 files changed, 182 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/engines/scumm/charset.cpp b/engines/scumm/charset.cpp
index c4c79c65..b3ae71e2 100644
--- a/engines/scumm/charset.cpp
+++ b/engines/scumm/charset.cpp
@@ -430,6 +430,11 @@ void ScummEngine::loadKorTtfMap(const Common::Path &mapPath) {
 	if (map.getKey("metrics", "latin", value))
 		_korTtfMetrics = value.equalsIgnoreCase("ttf");
 
+	// [render] mode=string draws whole runs at once instead of one glyph
